     "text": "```python\nfrom pedantic import validate\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nclass Library:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._books: List[str] = []\n\n    @validate\n    def add_books(self, books: List[str]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Adds a list of books to the library.\n\n        Args:\n            books (List[str]): A list of book titles to add.\n\n        Raises:\n            TypeError: If 'books' is not a list.\n            ValueError: If any book title is not a string.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(books, list):\n            raise TypeError(\"Books must be a list of strings.\")\n        for book in books:\n            if not isinstance(book, str):\n                raise ValueError(f\"Book title '{book}' must be a string.\")\n        self._books.extend(books)\n\n    @validate\n    def remove_books(self, books: List[str]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Removes a list of books from the library.\n\n        Args:\n            books (List[str]): A list of book titles to remove.\n\n        Raises:\n            TypeError: If 'books' is not a list.\n            ValueError: If any book title is not a string or does not exist in the library.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(books, list):\n            raise TypeError(\"Books must be a list of strings.\")\n        for book in books:\n            if not isinstance(book, str):\n                raise ValueError(f\"Book title '{book}' must be a string.\")\n            if book not in self._books:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Book title '{book}' does not exist in the library.\")\n        self._books = [book for book in self._books if book not in books]\n```",
